__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
# Output of `pip install .` (pip builds in the source tree).
build/
dist/

# Large, licensed or machine-local artifacts: never commit these. Several have caused an
# accidental multi-GB commit when added via `git add -A` or the GitHub web upload UI.
# Regenerate them locally (docs/reproducibility.md) instead.
# (gitignore has no trailing comments: every comment sits on its own line.)

# Trained model checkpoints (the removed RAG2 filter-reproduction attempt).
checkpoints/
# Local GGUF model files.
models/
ram_monitor.csv
# Local leftovers of the first design, removed from the repository on 2026-10-06: the retrieval index
# (~12.5 GB), the corpus text (multi-GB, at the repository root) and, inside the removed _archive folder,
# the filter-training labels (16.6 h of compute) and the corpus data. A computer that built them still holds
# them after a `git pull`, and `git add -A` must never pick them up. The leading slash anchors /corpus/ to the
# repository root.
experiments/results/index/
experiments/results/index_pilot_reduced_scope/
/corpus/
_archive/

# MedChange-derived questions, fetched PubMed abstracts, frozen candidate pools and raw
# working outputs. The MedChange release states no licence and abstracts are publisher
# text, so they are rebuilt from the manifest, not redistributed. Results worth keeping
# are copied to experiments/medchange/results/ (tracked) - see docs/reproducibility.md.
experiments/medchange/data/

# The same folders at their location BEFORE the 2026-10-02 reorganisation. Nothing is
# tracked there any more; the entry stays so leftover local files can never be committed.
experiments/baseline/

# Local data of the archived Alzheimer's question-set builder (publisher text); the code is in Git history, see docs/protocol.md section 8.
experiments/adkqa/data/
